From 3b07251b5967bca19905355663e1eb2f89f7af60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homar <homar@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:23:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] homalawn quiet link: no status notification, no foreground
 service

The link (TLS server, mDNS, unlock receiver) runs in the launcher's process from its start
(LinkService.ensureLink, once per process), not inside a foreground service. Nothing stays in the
notification shade: the owner wants notifications only when he has to do something.

What keeps the link reachable: Homa Lawn is the default home app, so Android keeps its process at
home-app priority behind other apps (never cached or frozen); with "Keep connected" (the battery
optimisation exemption) it also has network in Doze and its plain, sticky LinkService is not
stopped when the app goes idle. A process started without the home screen (crash alarm, boot,
update) starts the link the same way.

What the status notification did moves:
- "Set as home" and "Keep connected": LinkAsks posts one notification only while one of them is
  missing, each need once (dismissed, it stays away until that need comes back); removed when
  nothing is missing. Checked at link start and every time the home screen comes to the front.
- "Pair a computer": a "Pair a computer" row in Homa Lawn's settings opens the pairing screen
  (waiting for a computer, Forget all computers).
- "Connected" and "Screen control in use": no longer shown.

The old "omalawn_link" channel is deleted; the connectedDevice service type and its permission go,
and with them the debug_refuse_foreground hook. debug_link_state reports what LinkAsks would ask.
